  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup almond flour",
    "2 tablespoon flaxseed meal",
    "1/3 cup unsweetened carton coconut milk",
    "2 large egg",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "2 tablespoon stevia/erythritol blend (such as Swerve)",
    "7 drop liquid stevia",
    "3 ounce brie cheese (double cream)",
    "2 tablespoon butter",
    "1 tablespoon stevia/erythritol blend (such as Swerve)",
    "1/2 cup raspberries",
    "1 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "1 teaspoon lemon zest"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Mix together all of the waffle ingredients in a large mixing bowl. Make sure that the consistency is smooth and without any lumps.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6361.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat up a waffle maker and pour in the batter once hot. Allow it to cook until the indicator goes off or by using the steam method I described.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6365.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the waffles and let cool slightly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6374.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the brie and lay it on top of the waffles while still warm to help bring the brie to room temperature.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6389.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a pan on the stove, heat up the butter and sweetener. Optional: Use a spice grinder to powder the sweetener for better texture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6392.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the butter is beginning to brown and the sweetener is dissolving, add in the raspberries, lemon juice, and lemon zest.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6394.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue to stir the mixture until bubbling and jamlike in consistency.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6412.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Broil the waffles until they're slightly crisp and the brie has melted.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6418.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Assemble the waffles with the raspberry filling and brie. Place in a pan and toast for 1–2 minutes per side.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_6434.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/raspberry-brie-grilled-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51455-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
